{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SSXQFahn9C5fLWiohqULeq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Olympiyikes!\n2\t\n3\t**Tagline:** *Faster. Higher. Yikes.*\n4\t**One line:** the complete Summer *and* Winter Games, held in the same fortnight in one twin-city host, played as\n5\tan over-the-top arcade multi-event: 12 events, 8 nations, ceremonies, a rival, two hyperventilating commentators,\n6\t1–4 players on the couch and AI Hub ghost heats online.\n7\t\n8\t> **How the title was picked (TASK.md rule):** 50 riffs on \"Olympic Games\" were brainstormed silently, then\n9\t> `secrets.randbelow(50)` (Python, OS CSPRNG) returned **16 → \"Olympiyikes!\"**. Do not re-roll it. Its file-name\n10\t> form is `Olympiyikes`; the SOURCE token is `OlympicGames`.\n11\t\n12\t---\n13\t\n14\t## 0. Read this first (ground rules for the builders)\n15\t\n16\t- **Inputs:** `TASK.md` (requirements) + this plan. If they disagree, TASK.md wins. Where this plan is silent, follow\n17\t  the engine's own docs (`API.md`, `AI_GUIDE.md`) and the plan's spirit. Everything listed here ships: **no TODOs,\n18\t  placeholders, locked \"coming soon\" slots or stubbed features.**\n19\t- **Names (with this TASK.md):** dev folder `Olympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837/`, deliverable\n20\t  `Olympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837.html` in the root (beside TASK.md), and\n21\t  `exit-interview.json` in the root. If your TASK.md's name pattern carries a different model/date, use your pattern\n22\t  with `Olympiyikes` and `OlympicGames`.\n23\t- **Shared machine:** read only the files you need (other agents share the parent directories, ports and processes).\n24\t  Prefer `file://` and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), run\n25\t  `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` from your dev folder, read the port it prints, and confirm the served page\n26\t  is *your* game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by PID. Never `pkill`, `killall`,\n27\t  `fuser -k`. During planning `/tmp` was 100% full: if npm/Playwright fail with ENOSPC, set `TMPDIR=<dev>/.tmp`.\n28\t- **Engine:** my-3D2dge handoff package, **v0.85.2** at planning time\n29\t  (`https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff`). We own our copy and may change it (§4.6).\n30\t- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client **1.4.0** (`https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub`).\n31\t- **No subagents/workflows to debate, review, judge or audit** (TASK.md). Tests are scripts.\n32\t- **Units used in this plan:** world units (u) are the engine's (one tile = 16 u, z is up). Distances shown to the\n33\t  player are meters; each event says its scale (default **M = 12 u per meter**). Times in seconds unless marked ms.\n34\t  The engine runs fixed steps of 1/120 s.\n35\t\n36\t### 0.1 Fetch what you build on (once, inside the dev folder)\n37\t\n38\t```sh\n39\tD=Olympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837 && mkdir -p $D/{engine,src,tests,tools,vendor/hub,.tmp} && cd $D\n40\tgit clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git vendor/my-3d2dge\n41\tgit -C vendor/my-3d2dge sparse-checkout set dist/handoff\n42\tcp vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js engine/my-3d2dge.js          # our engine copy (we edit this one)\n43\tfor f in session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js README.md; do\n44\t  curl -fsSL -o vendor/hub/$f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f; done\n45\t(cd vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && export TMPDIR=\"$(cd ../../../.. && pwd)/.tmp\" && npm install && npx playwright install chromium)\n46\t```\n47\t\n48\tRead whole: `vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/API.md`, `README.md`, `kits/README.md`, `docs/ASSETS.md`,\n49\t`vendor/hub/README.md`. Read as references (copy patterns, not whole files): `kits/sports.js` (hockey), `kits/road.js`\n50\t(downhill/bobsled), `kits/rhythm.js` (figure skating), `kits/pinball.js` + `modules/physics.js` (curling),\n51\t`kits/kart.js` (drawing a rig through a custom view), `modules/arcade.js` (record tables, initials), `game/test.mjs`\n52\tand `kits/test.mjs` (headless harness). Grep `API-INDEX.md` for names; don't read it whole.\n53\t\n54\t---\n55\t\n56\t## 1. The game\n57\t\n58\t### 1.1 Pitch\n59\t\n60\tFor the first time in history the Summer and Winter Games share one fortnight and one host: **Mount Glory–Sunny Bay**,\n61\twhere a ski jump towers over the beach and the swimming pool shares a wall with the ice rink. Eight fictional nations\n62\tsend their stars. You pick a nation and its athlete, light the cauldron, and chase gold across **12 events** that\n63\talternate summer and winter, while defending champion **Max Overdrive of Turbonia** insists, loudly, that it is all\n64\tpointless because he will win. Everything is broadcast like the real thing (parade of nations, \"Up Close & Personal\"\n65\tprofiles, photo finishes, medal ceremonies with anthems, a medal table) and played like an arcade cabinet (mashing,\n66\ttiming, aiming, steering, rhythm, physics; a HYPE meter that sets you on fire; world records that explode into\n67\tfireworks). When it goes wrong, it goes *gloriously* wrong: false starts, belly flops, ski-jump tumbles, bobsleds on\n68\ttheir roof. That's an **OLYMPIYIKES!**, and the game celebrates it.\n69\t\n70\t### 1.2 Pillars\n71\t\n72\t1. **Ten seconds to learn, a lifetime to perfect.** Each event teaches one verb (mash, time, aim, steer, keep the beat,\n73\t   sweep) on one card, and has a perfect-play ceiling with world records to chase.\n74\t2. **Broadcast spectacle.** Ceremonies, commentators, crowd, jumbotron, slow-mo, photo finishes, anthems, records.\n75\t3. **Failure is a show.** Every event has at least one comic \"Yikes\" moment that is funny, fast to recover from, and\n76\t   even pays a little hype (§5.8).\n77\t4. **Both seasons.** 6 summer + 6 winter events on alternating days; each venue has its own look, light and music.\n78\t5. **Couch first, online too.** 1–4 local players in every mode; AI Hub ghost heats when the hub launches the game.\n79\t\n80\t### 1.3 Genre and perspective (decisions)\n81\t\n82\t- **Genre:** arcade multi-event sports (Track & Field / Winter Games lineage) with a short campaign, local party\n83\t  play and online ghost heats. Each event is a compact mini-game built on one shared event framework.\n84\t- **Perspective:** per event, all on the engine's native 2D views (pixel art at `res: 'ps1'`, `expand: true`):\n85\t  - **2.5D side-on lanes** (`'brawler'` view, pitch 25): 100m Dash, Javelin, 50m Freestyle, Weightlifting.\n86\t  - **Pure side view** (`'side'`): 10m Diving, Ski Jump, the archer's inset.\n87\t  - **Target close-up overlay:** Archery's main view.\n88\t  - **Pseudo-3D behind the athlete** (the `road` module, `E.Road`): Downhill, Bobsled.\n89\t  - **Three-quarter** (`'threequarter'`): Figure Skating, Ice Hockey.\n90\t  - Ceremonies, podiums and the title use `'brawler'` in their venue.\n91\t  - **Top-down** (`'topdown'`): Curling.\n92\t  Rationale: each event gets the camera its classic arcade ancestors used, and the engine has a native, tested view\n93\t  for every one of them.\n94\t\n95\t### 1.4 Core loop\n96\t\n97\tPick nation → (ceremony) → **day card** (who, where, a human-interest segment) → **event card** (one screen: goal and\n98\tcontrols with button glyphs) → **compete** (live vs CPU rivals and friends) → **results** (records, qualifying) →\n99\t**medal ceremony** → **medal table** (story beat) → next day. 12 days, then the closing ceremony and an ending that\n100\tdepends on your nation's rank.\n101\t\n102\t### 1.5 Modes (main menu, in this order)\n103\t\n104\t| Item | What it is |\n105\t|---|---|\n106\t| CONTINUE GAMES | only when an autosave exists: resumes The Games at the next day |\n107\t| THE GAMES | the campaign: opening ceremony, 12 days (all 12 events), story beats, halftime report, closing ceremony, ending; or, chosen on its setup screen, **Quick Games**: 4 events (playlists *Track & Pool*, *Snow & Ice*, *Greatest Hits*, *Random 4*) with mini ceremonies and party points. 1–4 players |\n108\t| SINGLE EVENT | any of the 12 events, vs CPU or practice (no rivals); 1–4 players |\n109\t| RECORDS | world records and top-5 tables per event (initials), the Laurel cabinet, the Medal cabinet |\n110\t| HOW TO PLAY | Basics (mash, timing, hype & turbo, yikes) + every event's card |\n111\t| SETTINGS | the engine's settings screen plus the game's own (§2.5) |\n112\t| ABOUT & CREDITS | Source Information, Testing/Engine/Prompt Feedback, credits, engine changes, controls |\n113\t\n114\tOnline play is not a menu item: it starts only when the AI Hub launches the page (§12.2).\n115\t\n116\t---\n117\t\n118\t## 2. Controls and input (controller-first, keyboard and mouse native)\n119\t\n120\t### 2.1 The action map (custom preset `OLY_KEYS`, replaces the engine presets for the whole game)\n121\t\n122\t| Action | Meaning | DualSense (default glyphs) | Xbox glyphs (setting) | Keyboard | Mouse |\n123\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n124\t| `up/down/left/right` | move, steer, aim, balance, menu focus | left stick, d-pad | left stick, d-pad | WASD, arrows | — |\n125\t| `mashL` | \"left\": left foot/arm, push, pass, tuck (diving), in-turn | □ and L1 | X and LB | **J** | — |\n126\t| `mashR` | \"right\": right foot/arm, push, check, pike (diving), out-turn | ○ and R1 | B and RB | **K** | — |\n127\t| `action` | jump, throw, release, start, take-off, shoot | ✕ | A | **Space** | Left button (aim events only) |\n128\t| `turbo` | fire the YIKES TURBO when the hype flame is full | △ | Y | **Shift** | — |\n129\t| `alt` | hold: tuck, breathe, hold breath, skate burst | R2 (and L2) | RT (and LT) | **L** | Right button (aim events only) |\n130\t| `pause` | pause menu | Options | Menu | Esc, P | — |\n131\t| `confirm` | menus: choose | ✕ | A | Enter, Space | click |\n132\t| `cancel` | menus: back | ○ | B | Esc, Backspace | — |\n133\t\n134\tRules:\n135\t- **`confirm`/`cancel` deliberately do not include J or K** (the engine's DEFAULT preset has them): a sprinter mashing J/K\n136\t  must never skip a results screen. Every screen entered after play has a **0.6 s input lockout** and calls\n137\t  `input.consumeAll()` on enter.\n138\t- **Mash = alternate `mashL` and `mashR`.** PC players mash J/K with the right hand; pad players rock □/○ with a thumb\n139\t  or alternate L1/R1 with index fingers (both pairs are bound). Mash assist (§2.5) offers one-button and hold modes.\n140\t- **Mouse:** menus everywhere (hover moves the focus, click picks; `E.Menu` does this, our widgets copy it). In-world\n141\t  only where the genre uses it: Archery (pointer aims, hold left to draw/release to shoot, hold right to hold breath),\n142\t  Curling (pointer aims the broom target, left button = `action`), Hockey (left: hold/release shoot toward the\n143\t  cursor, right: pass toward the cursor), plus clicking flags on Nation Select and tiles on Single Event. Those event\n144\t  scenes set their own `input` preset that adds `Mouse0`/`Mouse2`; other scenes leave the mouse unbound in play.\n145\t- **Pause and the hub:** in an AI Hub session, \"Create + Options\" belongs to the hub: while pad button 8 (Create) is\n146\t  held, suppress `pause` *before* the engine reads it (needs the exported input hook, §4.6 change 1).\n147\t- Two players on one keyboard: the engine's `game.allowJoin` splits it (P1 WASD + F G H R T Y, P2 arrows + `.` `/` `,`\n148\t  and numpad); our actions map onto the halves in preset order (`mashL, mashR, action, turbo, alt`). Prompts follow\n149\t  automatically because every prompt comes from `input.label(action)`.\n150\t\n151\t### 2.2 Per-event use of the actions\n152\t\n153\t| Event | stick / WASD | mashL □ J | mashR ○ K | action ✕ Space | turbo △ Shift | alt R2 L | mouse |\n154\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n155\t| 100m Dash | — | left foot | right foot | react at the gun; dip at the line | turbo | — | — |\n156\t| Javelin | — | run | run | hold: angle rises; release: throw | turbo | — | — |\n157\t| 50m Freestyle | — | left arm (on the beat) | right arm (on the beat) | start dive, flip turn, touch | turbo | breathe | — |\n158\t| 10m Diving | tap ←/→: half twist | hold: tuck | hold: pike | take-off timing | turbo | — | — |\n159\t| Archery | aim | — | — | hold: draw; release: shoot | turbo | hold: hold breath | pointer aims, L draw, R breath |\n160\t| Weightlifting | ←/→ balance | lift | lift | jerk timing | turbo | — | — |\n161\t| Ski Jump | ↑/↓ balance, body angle | — | — | push off, take-off, telemark | turbo | — | — |\n162\t| Downhill | steer | — | — | pre-jump | turbo | hold: tuck | — |\n163\t| Bobsled | steer | push | push | jump in (load) | turbo | — | — |\n164\t| Figure Skating | ← ↓ ↑ → notes | — | — | hold/release jump notes | turbo | — | — |\n165\t| Curling | aim | in-turn; sweep | out-turn; sweep | start slide; release | turbo | — | pointer aims, L = action |\n166\t| Ice Hockey | skate | pass | check / switch skater | hold: charge, release: shoot | ON FIRE | skate burst | L shoot at cursor, R pass at cursor |\n167\t\n168\t### 2.3 Button prompts and glyphs (a must-build: the pixel font has no ✕ ○ □ △)\n169\t\n170\t`input.label(action)` already returns the right *text* for the player's last device and bindings ('J', 'Space',\n171\t'Left click', '✕', 'A'...), and the engine's `glyphs` setting picks the controller family. But the engine's 5×7 pixel\n172\tfont has no ✕ ○ □ △ (they render as `?`). Build **`O.Prompt`** (src/02-prompts.js):\n173\t\n174\t- `O.Prompt.draw(g, x, y, action, { input = player's input, size: 1|2, label: 'RUN', align })` resolves the code\n175\t  for that player's `lastDevice` from `input.map`/`input.bindings`, then draws an **icon**, never plain text:\n176\t  - PlayStation face buttons: a 9×9 (size 1) / 17×17 (size 2) dark disc with a light rim and the symbol drawn in pixels\n177\t    in its traditional color (✕ blue `#7fb2ff`, ○ red `#ff6b6b`, □ pink `#ff8fd8`, △ green `#4fe0a8`).\n178\t  - Xbox face buttons: disc with the letter (A green `#5bc236`, B red `#e8443a`, X blue `#3a7cf0`, Y yellow `#f2c21b`).\n179\t  - Shoulders/triggers: rounded tab \"L1/R1/L2/R2\" or \"LB/RB/LT/RT\"; Options/Menu: small pill; sticks: a ring with an\n180\t    arrow; d-pad: a cross with the pressed arm lit.\n181\t  - Keyboard: a keycap (rounded rect, 1 px darker bottom edge) with the key's label; Space and Shift are wide caps.\n182\t  - Mouse: a mouse outline with the left/right half filled.\n183\t  - A pair prompt for mashing (`O.Prompt.pair(g, x, y, 'mashL', 'mashR')`) alternates highlight at the player's\n184\t    current mash rhythm (teaches the alternation).\n185\t- Prompts follow the **last input used, per player** (`input.lastDevice`); in multiplayer each lane/turn shows its\n186\t  own player's glyphs.\n187\t- **Default glyph family for controllers: PlayStation.** On first boot, if `game.settings.glyphs` is `'auto'` (never\n188\t  chosen) set it to `'playstation'` (engine change 4). The Settings → Game screen has **Controller prompts:\n189\t  PlayStation / Xbox** (key `promptStyle`) whose `apply` calls `game.settings.set('glyphs', v)`.\n190\t- Also add pixel glyphs for ✕ ○ □ △ to the engine's 5×7 and 3×5 fonts (engine change 3) so any stray label text\n191\t  still reads correctly.\n192\t\n193\t### 2.4 Menus\n194\t\n195\tStick/d-pad/WASD/arrows move the focus (with `input.repeat`); ✕/Enter/Space/click choose; ○/Esc/Backspace go back;\n196\tL1/R1 or Q/E switch tabs (also clickable); hovering with the mouse moves the focus. Every screen shows its prompt strip\n197\tat the bottom (`✕ Select  ○ Back`) with glyph icons.\n198\t\n199\t### 2.5 The game's settings (Settings → Game group, via `new E.Game({ menu: { settings: [...] } })`)\n200\t\n201\t| Key | Label | Options (default **bold**) |\n202\t|---|---|---|\n203\t| `difficulty` | Difficulty | Easy / **Normal** / Hard (CPU skill offset −0.12 / 0 / +0.06; timing windows ×1.25 / 1 / 0.85; qualifying standards per event) |\n204\t| `promptStyle` | Controller prompts | **PlayStation** / Xbox |\n205\t| `mashAssist` | Mash assist | **Off** / One button (any mash button counts as an alternation) / Hold (holding either = steady 72% pace) |\n206\t| `timingAssist` | Timing assist | **Off** / On (all timing windows ×1.4) |\n207\t| `commentary` | Commentary | **Voices + subtitles** / Subtitles only / Off |\n208\t| `textSize` | Text size | **Large** / Huge (×1.5 for subtitles, cards and HUD labels) |\n209\t| `hints` | Hints | **On** / Off (contextual tips, e.g. \"Alternate □ and ○!\") |\n210\t| `voices` | Voices volume (Sound group) | slider 0–1, **0.8** (engine change 6) |\n211\t| `crowd` | Crowd volume (Sound group) | slider 0–1, **0.7** |\n212\t\n213\tThe engine's own Display/Sound/Comfort/Controller/Touch settings, rebinding and full screen stay as they are\n214\t(TASK.md: don't rebuild standard features).\n215\t\n216\t---\n217\t\n218\t## 3. UI and UX (10-foot)\n219\t\n220\t### 3.1 Rules\n221\t\n222\t- **Base resolution** `res: 'ps1'` with `expand: true` (a 16:9 TV shows ~427×240 game pixels, scaled ×4.5 at 1080p).\n223\t  Primary text uses `E.font` at **scale 2** (≈63 px tall on a 1080p TV), secondary at scale 1 (≈31 px); never the\n224\t  `tiny` font for anything a player must read. Titles use `E.font.title` scale 4–5.\n225\t- **At most 7 items per list; at most 8 rows per table** (8 nations / 8 lanes). No scrolling tables, no web-style\n226\t  dense screens; long content is paged (L1/R1, ←/→ or clickable page dots).\n227\t- **Focus is loud:** the focused item has a gold bar, a ▸ cursor, a 1 px glow and a gentle scale pulse; a `select`\n228\t  blip on move, `confirm` on choose.\n229\t- **TV-safe margins:** keep HUD and text ≥ 12 game px from every edge; keep the top-right clear of\n230\t  `game.cornerArea()` (the engine's menu/full-screen buttons).\n231\t- **Anchoring:** every HUD element anchors to `r.W`/`r.H`; wide screens show more venue (more stands, more slope).\n232\t- **Information never in color alone:** players are P1–P4 tags plus color (`E.PLAYER_COLORS`), medals carry 1/2/3.\n233\t- **The engine's HTML screens** (pause, settings, controls) must be TV-readable: inject a stylesheet (no engine change)\n234\t  after the engine creates its shell, e.g. `.esh{font-size:clamp(16px,1.55vw,30px)} .esh button{font-size:1.15em;min-height:2.9em;padding:.7em 1em}\n235\t  .esh h2{font-size:2.2em} .esh-mod{width:min(820px,94vw)} .esh input[type=range]{width:min(320px,30vw);height:2.2em}`\n236\t  and theme it gold-on-navy via `E.Shell` theme variables (`accent: '#f2b632'`, `paper: 'rgba(12,16,40,.92)'`).\n237\t  Check with a 1920×1080 screenshot.\n238\t\n239\t### 3.2 Screens (all pixel art unless marked HTML)\n240\t\n241\t| # | Screen | Layout essentials |\n242\t|---|---|---|\n243\t| 1 | Boot (engine) | `boot: { title: 'OLYMPIYIKES!', steps: [...], messages: ['Inflating the blimp', 'Waxing the skis', 'Teaching the crowd to wave', 'Calming the mascot'] }` |\n244\t| 2 | Title | stadium at sunset (summer half) beside a floodlit ski jump (winter half), cauldron burning, blimp, the 8 athletes warming up in a row, logo `OLYMPIYIKES!` (E.font.title scale 5, gold→orange, red outline, depth 3), emblem, tagline, pulsing \"PRESS ✕\" (glyph by device), engine version tiny bottom-right. Idle 10 s → attract |\n245\t| 3 | Main menu | left: big list (§1.5); right: a live vignette for the focused item (parade / pictogram wheel / trophy / the mascot); bottom: description + prompt strip |\n246\t| 4 | Touch-only notice | replaces \"PRESS ✕\": panel **\"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\"**, one line \"Connect a controller or keyboard to play.\", a big **SETTINGS** button (tap → `game.menu('settings')`). Attract still runs |\n247\t| 5 | Games setup | rows: Length (Full 12 / Quick 4 + playlist), Difficulty, Qualifying (On for 1P / Off), START |\n248\t| 6 | Nation select + join | 4×2 grid of big flags (48×32) with codes; each player's cursor in its color with a P-tag; right panel: the focused nation's athlete (live rig cheering), name, 3 specialty pictograms, one-line bio; \"P2–P4: press ✕ on another controller, or 2 on the keyboard\" |\n249\t| 7 | Opening ceremony | cinematic (§7.4), hold ✕ for 1 s to skip |\n250\t| 8 | Day card (\"broadcast bumper\") | `DAY 3 · 50m FREESTYLE` / venue / weather; lower third: **UP CLOSE & PERSONAL** with a big portrait and 2–3 subtitle lines; optional rival line |\n251\t| 9 | Event card | pictogram + name; GOAL line; 3–4 rows of glyph icon(s) + verb; Qualifying standard, World record; prompts `✕ Start  ○ Back` (+ `△ Practice` in Single Event) |\n252\t| 10 | Event HUD | per event (§6); common: top-left event + pictogram, top-right clock/score (big digits), bottom: per-player prompt strip and the hype flame |\n253\t| 11 | Turn card | \"P2 — YOUR TURN\" in player color / \"ROUND 2 OF 3\" + top-4 standings |\n254\t| 12 | Results | ≤ 8 rows: rank, medal icon, flag, athlete, performance, notes (WR, GR, PB, Q, DNF, DQ); humans' rows in player color; records burst; `✕ Continue` |\n255\t| 13 | Initials entry | `E.Arcade` letter wheel when a human makes a top-5 table (skipped in hub) |\n256\t| 14 | Medal ceremony | podium in the venue, medals, three flags rising, the winner's procedural anthem, fireworks |\n257\t| 15 | Medal table | 8 nation rows (flag, code, G S B, total), yours highlighted; a ticker of the day's highlights |\n258\t| 16 | Story beat | day-card layout with one or two portraits (halftime report, incidents, rival) |\n259\t| 17 | Torch lost / Games over | \"YIKES! NO QUALIFYING MARK — TORCHES ●●○\" → retry; at 0: \"GAMES OVER — CONTINUE? 9\" |\n260\t| 18 | Closing + ending + credits | cinematic, ending text by rank, credits roll (paged, skippable) |\n261\t| 19 | Single Event select | 4×3 grid of event tiles (pictogram, name, season color, your best medal); bottom: description |\n262\t| 20 | Records | tabs per event (←/→ or L1/R1): top-5 rows; tabs LAURELS (12 tiles) and CABINET (nation × event medals as icons) |\n263\t| 21 | How to play | Basics pages + list of 12 event cards (read-only) |\n264\t| 22 | Settings / Controls / Pause | engine HTML (scaled, themed) |\n265\t| 23 | About & Credits | paged: Source Information · Testing Feedback · Engine Feedback · Prompt Feedback · Credits & engine changes · Controls |\n266\t| 24 | Dev panel | pixel overlay (§13) |\n267\t| 25 | Hub card / hub splash | §12.2 |\n268\t\n269\tTransitions: `game.go(scene, data, { fade: 'wipe' })` between menu screens, `'iris'` into events, `'white'` into\n270\tceremonies (reduce-motion turns them into plain fades by itself).\n271\t\n272\t### 3.3 Touch-only devices\n273\t\n274\t`touchOnly = matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches\n275\t&& navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0` **and** no key press or gamepad has been seen this visit. While true: show screen 4,\n276\thide engine touch buttons (scenes declare `touch: []`; set the engine's `touch` setting to `'off'` at boot),\n277\tlet the attract mode run after 10 s; a tap during attract returns to the notice. A `gamepadconnected` event or any key\n278\tpress flips `touchOnly` to false at once and shows the normal title.\n279\t\n280\t---\n281\t\n282\t## 4. Architecture\n283\t\n284\t### 4.1 Tech stack\n285\t\n286\t- **Engine:** our copy of the my-3D2dge v0.85.2 full engine (`engine/my-3d2dge.js`: the core plus every module; we use\n287\t  the `road`, `rhythm`, `physics`, `arcade` and `songs` modules from it). Plain JavaScript, no libraries, no CDN, no\n288\t  network at runtime.\n289\t- **Online:** AI Hub `session.js` 1.4.0, unmodified, first script in `<head>`.\n290\t- **Tooling:** Node (headless tests via `vm`, as `game/test.mjs` does), Playwright 1.63.0 + Chromium (browser checks,\n291\t  hub harness, screenshots), the handoff's `tools/check.mjs` and `tools/filmstrip.mjs`.\n292\t- **Deliverable:** one self-contained HTML (engine + session client + game inlined), ~1.8 MB, works from `file://`.\n293\t\n294\t### 4.2 Folder layout\n295\t\n296\t```\n297\tOlympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837/\n298\t  index.html                 dev page: same <head> as the bundle; loads engine + src files in order (the list is the bundle's source of truth)\n299\t  engine/my-3d2dge.js        the engine + our changes, each marked  // OLY: <why>\n300\t  vendor/hub/                session.js (bundled, unmodified) + harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md (tests only)\n301\t  vendor/my-3d2dge/          sparse clone of the handoff: docs, kits, tools (reference + Playwright); never bundled\n302\t  src/                       the game: one IIFE per file, all attach to window.OLY (alias O)\n303\t  tests/                     run.mjs (the one command) + suites\n304\t  tools/bundle.mjs           builds the root HTML from index.html's script list\n305\t  tools/shots.mjs            screenshot/filmstrip helper around the handoff tools\n306\t```\n307\t\n308\t### 4.3 Source files (load order = bundle order)\n309\t\n310\t| File | Responsibility |\n311\t|---|---|\n312\t| `00-core.js` | creates `window.OLY`, defines `OLY_KEYS` and `GAME_SETTINGS`, then the `E.Game` (§4.4), constants (`M`, palettes), `O.def(kind, id, spec)` registries, `O.bus` (on/emit), `O.store` (E.store wrappers), `O.rng(label)` streams (§4.7), formatting helpers |\n313\t| `01-input.js` | per-scene presets (archery/curling/hockey add mouse), **pilots** (§5.2), `Mash` meter, `O.AutoPlayer` (bot intents → real `input.tap/hold`), idle/any-input tracker, touch-only detection, hub Create+Options guard |\n314\t| `02-prompts.js` | `O.Prompt` glyph renderer (§2.3) |\n315\t| `03-ui.js` | 10-foot widgets: `Menu10` (vertical list), `Grid10` (tile grid), `Tabs`, `Panel`, `Banner` (big stamped words), `Ticker`, `LowerThird`, `Toast`, page dots, number/time formatters; mouse hover/click via `input.pointer()`/`clicked()` |\n316\t| `04-audio.js` | SFX definitions (`audio.define`), songs (§9), `O.Voice` gibberish synth, `O.CrowdAudio`, `O.Anthem` generator, stings |\n317\t| `05-art.js` | palettes per venue, flag painter, pictograms, emblem, equipment sprites, stands + crowd painter, jumbotron (dot matrix), podium, fireworks/confetti helpers, mascot (Blob) |\n318\t| `06-pose.js` | `O.Pose` library and `O.Gear` (equipment drawn at joints), body rotation (§8.2) |\n319\t| `07-athletes.js` | `NATIONS` data (§7.1), teammates, `O.makeRig(nation, sport, opts)` outfits per sport, voice params |\n320\t| `08-commentary.js` | `O.Comms`: commentators, line banks (§7.6), cue rules, subtitles + voice + portraits |\n321\t| `09-hype.js` | `O.Hype` (meter, turbo), `O.Yikes` (stamp, count, sympathy hype), `O.Crowd` (visual excitement), slow-mo/photo helpers |\n322\t| `10-records.js` | world records seed table, games records, personal bests, top-5 tables via `E.Arcade`, points formulas, medal table, party points, laurels, cabinet |\n323\t| `11-ghosts.js` | ghost recording/playback (local turns + hub), compact samples |\n324\t| `12-eventkit.js` | the event contract, `O.defEvent`, the phase runner, formats (race / attempts / match / program), CPU simulation, results assembly, qualifying, timing widgets (`TimingBar`, `Ring`, `Balance`, `Sway`, `StrokeBeat`) |\n325\t| `20-ev-sprint.js` … `35-ev-hockey.js` | one file per event (§6), ids: `sprint javelin swim diving archery weights skijump downhill bobsled figure curling hockey` |\n326\t| `40-sc-title.js` | title, main menu, touch-only notice, attract director (§11) |\n327\t| `41-sc-games.js` | games setup, nation select/join, opening ceremony, day card, story beats, event card, turn card, results, initials, medal ceremony, medal table, torch/continue, closing + ending + credits |\n328\t| `42-sc-misc.js` | single event select, records, how to play, about & credits, pose lab |\n329\t| `43-dev.js` | dev panel, tuning sliders, cheats, overlays (§13) |\n330\t| `44-hub.js` | AI Hub session flow (§12.2) |\n331\t| `99-main.js` | registers scenes, deep links (`#ev/<id>`, `#scene/<name>`, `#attract`, `#poselab`, `#games/day/<n>`), `game.debug`, `window.__oly` for tests, `game.start({ scenes, scene, boot })` |\n332\t\n333\tEach file: `(() => { 'use strict'; const E = My3D2dge, O = OLY; ... })();`. Tests load exactly the same files in the same\n334\torder into a `vm` context (read the list from `index.html` so it can't drift).\n335\t\n336\t### 4.4 The game object\n337\t\n338\t```js\n339\tconst game = O.game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'brawler', input: OLY_KEYS,\n340\t  id: 'olympiyikes', bg: '#0b0f24',\n341\t  menu: { items: inHub ? [] : [['Restart event', () => O.restartEvent()], ['How to play', () => O.showEventCard()], ['Dev mode', () => O.Dev.open()]],\n342\t          settings: GAME_SETTINGS /* §2.5 */, quit: inHub ? false : 'title',\n343\t          controls: { mashL: 'Left (mash, pass, tuck)', mashR: 'Right (mash, check, pike)', action: 'Action (jump, throw, release)',\n344\t                      turbo: 'Yikes Turbo', alt: 'Hold (tuck, breathe, steady)' } } });\n345\t```\n346\t`inHub = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active)` (true from the client's first line). `OLY_KEYS` and `GAME_SETTINGS` are defined\n347\tin `00-core.js` above this call (the later files only add to them); the menu callbacks are arrows because their targets\n348\tare defined in later files. Menu items are static, so each item's\n349\tfunction is context-aware: outside an event \"Restart event\" and \"How to play\" show `game.note('Not in an event')`.\n350\t\n351\t### 4.5 Scenes\n352\t\n353\t`O.scene(name, def)` registers a wrapped engine scene. The wrapper: calls `input.consumeAll()` on enter; applies the\n354\t0.6 s lockout (`def.lock`); if the dev panel is open, runs `O.Dev.update()` instead of `def.update` and draws the panel\n355\tafter `def.draw`; draws global overlays (toasts, commentary lower third, attract banner, \"YIKES\" stamps, laurel toasts)\n356\tafter the scene; tracks idle time on menu scenes (`def.menu: true`) for the attract mode; routes `back()`.\n357\t\n358\tScenes: `title`, `menu`, `touchonly` (a state of `title`), `attract`, `gamesSetup`, `nations`, `opening`, `dayCard`,\n359\t`beat`, `eventCard`, `turnCard` (overlay state inside events), `ev:<id>` ×12, `results`, `initials`, `podium`,\n360\t`medals`, `torch`, `closing`, `credits`, `single`, `records`, `howto`, `about`, `poselab`, `hubCard`, `hubSplash`.\n361\t\n362\t`O.flow` is the state machine above them: it holds the current **meet** (§4.8) and decides the next scene after each\n363\tone ends (`O.flow.next(from, payload)`), for each mode (games, quick, single, hub, attract).\n364\t\n365\t### 4.6 Engine changes (all marked `// OLY:` in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`; list them on the About screen)\n366\t\n367\t1. **Export the hooks:** `E.HOOKS = HOOKS;` so the game can run code at the start of every step even while paused\n368\t   (`HOOKS.input`): hub Create+Options guard, global any-input detection.\n369\t2. **Cosmetic randomness off `Math.random`:** the Humanoid (`this.t` start phase, blink timer), `Particles` and\n370\t   `hitFx`'s number jitter draw from a module-level `const cosmetic = rng(0xC05E7)` instead of `Math.random`. Then\n371\t   cosmetics never shift gameplay randomness, the hub card draws no `Math.random` numbers, and tests stay\n372\t   deterministic.\n373\t3. **Font glyphs:** add ✕ ○ □ △ to the 5×7 (`G57`) and 3×5 (`GLYPHS`) tables.\n374\t4. **PlayStation by default:** the `glyphs` setting's default becomes `'playstation'`.\n375\t5. **Pose hook on the Humanoid:** at the end of `solvePose()`, if `this.post` is a function call `this.post(this, this.J)`;\n376\t   then, if `this.bodyPitch || this.bodyRoll`, rotate every joint (and cape/hair points, as `_roll` does) about\n377\t   `this.pivot` (default: hip centre) by pitch (forward–up plane) and roll (right–up plane), **without** `_roll`'s\n378\t   floor lift. This is what flips, dives, swims, tumbles and V-style flight need (§8.2).\n379\t6. **Voice bus:** `ChipAudio` gets a `_voiceBus` gain under the master, a `voiceVolume` field honored by\n380\t   `applyVolume()`, and the settings get `voices` (Sound group, default .8). `O.Voice` connects to it.\n381\t\n382\t### 4.7 Randomness and determinism\n383\t\n384\t- **Gameplay randomness only through labeled streams:** `O.rng(label)` returns a `[0,1)` generator. In a hub session\n385\t  it is `AIHub.rng(label)` (identical on every copy); otherwise `E.rng(hash(meet.seed + '|' + label))`. Labels are\n386\t  namespaced: `'sprint:gun'`, `'javelin:wind:r2'`, `'cpu:FRM:skijump:j1'`, `'judges:diving:SUN:d3'`.\n387\t- Cosmetics (particles, blinks, crowd bob) never touch `Math.random` (engine change 2) or the gameplay streams.\n388\t- `meet.seed` comes from the clock when a meet starts; tests and the dev panel can set it.\n389\t- Every event sim is a function of (state, intents, streams), independent of drawing, so a sim can run headless,\n390\t  twice, and hash the same (the kits' \"proof\" idea).\n391\t\n392\t### 4.8 Data model\n393\t\n394\t```\n395\tNation   { id: 'SUN', name: 'SUNVALE', colors: { a, b, c }, flag: { kind, ... }, athlete: { name, rig, bio, voice },\n396\t           team: [3 names], skills: { sprint: .92, ... }, anthem: { seed, key, bpm } }\n397\tAthlete  { id, nation, name, rig, gear, pilot, lane, human, player (0-3 | null), hype, turboT, state: {}, attempts: [],\n398\t           best, notes: [], ghost }\n399\tPilot    { kind: 'human' | 'bot' | 'ghost' | 'net', input?, skill, cheat?: 'perfect' | null }\n400\tIntent   { L, R, A, T (pressed this step), Lh, Rh, Ad, Au, X (held / released), mv: [x, y], aim: [x, y] | null }\n401\tMeet     { mode, seed, events: [ids], day, players: [{ input, nation, color }], difficulty, qualifying, torches,\n402\t           medals: { SUN: { g, s, b } }, party: { P1: pts }, results: { eventId: Results }, beats: Set, yikes: { SUN: n } }\n403\tResults  { event, rows: [{ athlete, perf, display, rank, medal, notes, points }], records: [], laurels: [] }\n404\tStore    'oly:records' (top-5 per event + WR), 'oly:laurels', 'oly:cabinet', 'oly:games' (autosave),\n405\t         'oly:ghost:<event>' (best local run), 'oly:seen' (first-time tips), 'oly:tune' (only if the dev opts in)\n406\t```\n407\t\n408\t### 4.9 Bundle\n409\t\n410\t`node tools/bundle.mjs` reads `index.html`'s `<script src>` list and writes the root HTML:\n411\t\n412\t```html\n413\t<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n414\t<script>/* vendor/hub/session.js, byte-for-byte */</script>\n415\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n416\t<title>Olympiyikes! — Faster. Higher. Yikes.</title>\n417\t<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Twelve over-the-top Summer and Winter events in one wild fortnight, for 1–4 players.\">\n418\t<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#f2b632\"><link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:image/svg+xml,...the emblem...\">\n419\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"><meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n420\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Score the most points across three Olympiyikes events\">\n421\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move · □○ or J K mash · ✕/Space act · △/Shift turbo · R2/L hold\">\n422\t<meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"The Olympic Games\"><meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"(the building model's id)\">\n423\t<style>/* page + 10-foot shell overrides */</style></head><body>\n424\t<!-- E.bootSplash('OLYMPIYIKES!') markup --><canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n425\t<script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js */</script><script>/* src/*.js concatenated */</script></body></html>\n426\t```\n427\tEscape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\/script`. The session client must stay unmodified and first after\n428\t`<meta charset>`. The bundle test (§16) checks all of this.\n429\t\n430\t---\n431\t\n432\t## 5. Shared gameplay systems\n433\t\n434\t### 5.1 The event contract (`O.defEvent`) and the phase runner\n435\t\n436\tEvery event is one call. The EventKit turns it into an engine scene `ev:<id>`, registers it in `O.EVENTS`, its\n437\ttunables in the tuning registry (§5.13), its card in How to Play, its segment in the attract playlist and, if\n438\t`hub.ok`, in the hub deal.\n439\t\n440\t```js"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0d39672-91d7-4659-90e6-59a7cf2c42a6","uuid":"b96e6a1b-0947-47bb-a9a4-47d491efda2c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:44:47.700Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-074439__x0e4b02/work/PLAN.md","content":"# Olympiyikes!\n\n**Tagline:** *Faster. Higher. Yikes.*\n**One line:** the complete Summer *and* Winter Games, held in the same fortnight in one twin-city host, played as\nan over-the-top arcade multi-event: 12 events, 8 nations, ceremonies, a rival, two hyperventilating commentators,\n1–4 players on the couch and AI Hub ghost heats online.\n\n> **How the title was picked (TASK.md rule):** 50 riffs on \"Olympic Games\" were brainstormed silently, then\n> `secrets.randbelow(50)` (Python, OS CSPRNG) returned **16 → \"Olympiyikes!\"**. Do not re-roll it. Its file-name\n> form is `Olympiyikes`; the SOURCE token is `OlympicGames`.\n\n---\n\n## 0. Read this first (ground rules for the builders)\n\n- **Inputs:** `TASK.md` (requirements) + this plan. If they disagree, TASK.md wins. Where this plan is silent, follow\n  the engine's own docs (`API.md`, `AI_GUIDE.md`) and the plan's spirit. Everything listed here ships: **no TODOs,\n  placeholders, locked \"coming soon\" slots or stubbed features.**\n- **Names (with this TASK.md):** dev folder `Olympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837/`, deliverable\n  `Olympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837.html` in the root (beside TASK.md), and\n  `exit-interview.json` in the root. If your TASK.md's name pattern carries a different model/date, use your pattern\n  with `Olympiyikes` and `OlympicGames`.\n- **Shared machine:** read only the files you need (other agents share the parent directories, ports and processes).\n  Prefer `file://` and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), run\n  `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` from your dev folder, read the port it prints, and confirm the served page\n  is *your* game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by PID. Never `pkill`, `killall`,\n  `fuser -k`. During planning `/tmp` was 100% full: if npm/Playwright fail with ENOSPC, set `TMPDIR=<dev>/.tmp`.\n- **Engine:** my-3D2dge handoff package, **v0.85.2** at planning time\n  (`https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff`). We own our copy and may change it (§4.6).\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client **1.4.0** (`https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub`).\n- **No subagents/workflows to debate, review, judge or audit** (TASK.md). Tests are scripts.\n- **Units used in this plan:** world units (u) are the engine's (one tile = 16 u, z is up). Distances shown to the\n  player are meters; each event says its scale (default **M = 12 u per meter**). Times in seconds unless marked ms.\n  The engine runs fixed steps of 1/120 s.\n\n### 0.1 Fetch what you build on (once, inside the dev folder)\n\n```sh\nD=Olympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837 && mkdir -p $D/{engine,src,tests,tools,vendor/hub,.tmp} && cd $D\ngit clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git vendor/my-3d2dge\ngit -C vendor/my-3d2dge sparse-checkout set dist/handoff\ncp vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js engine/my-3d2dge.js          # our engine copy (we edit this one)\nfor f in session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js README.md; do\n  curl -fsSL -o vendor/hub/$f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f; done\n(cd vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && export TMPDIR=\"$(cd ../../../.. && pwd)/.tmp\" && npm install && npx playwright install chromium)\n```\n\nRead whole: `vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/API.md`, `README.md`, `kits/README.md`, `docs/ASSETS.md`,\n`vendor/hub/README.md`. Read as references (copy patterns, not whole files): `kits/sports.js` (hockey), `kits/road.js`\n(downhill/bobsled), `kits/rhythm.js` (figure skating), `kits/pinball.js` + `modules/physics.js` (curling),\n`kits/kart.js` (drawing a rig through a custom view), `modules/arcade.js` (record tables, initials), `game/test.mjs`\nand `kits/test.mjs` (headless harness). Grep `API-INDEX.md` for names; don't read it whole.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The game\n\n### 1.1 Pitch\n\nFor the first time in history the Summer and Winter Games share one fortnight and one host: **Mount Glory–Sunny Bay**,\nwhere a ski jump towers over the beach and the swimming pool shares a wall with the ice rink. Eight fictional nations\nsend their stars. You pick a nation and its athlete, light the cauldron, and chase gold across **12 events** that\nalternate summer and winter, while defending champion **Max Overdrive of Turbonia** insists, loudly, that it is all\npointless because he will win. Everything is broadcast like the real thing (parade of nations, \"Up Close & Personal\"\nprofiles, photo finishes, medal ceremonies with anthems, a medal table) and played like an arcade cabinet (mashing,\ntiming, aiming, steering, rhythm, physics; a HYPE meter that sets you on fire; world records that explode into\nfireworks). When it goes wrong, it goes *gloriously* wrong: false starts, belly flops, ski-jump tumbles, bobsleds on\ntheir roof. That's an **OLYMPIYIKES!**, and the game celebrates it.\n\n### 1.2 Pillars\n\n1. **Ten seconds to learn, a lifetime to perfect.** Each event teaches one verb (mash, time, aim, steer, keep the beat,\n   sweep) on one card, and has a perfect-play ceiling with world records to chase.\n2. **Broadcast spectacle.** Ceremonies, commentators, crowd, jumbotron, slow-mo, photo finishes, anthems, records.\n3. **Failure is a show.** Every event has at least one comic \"Yikes\" moment that is funny, fast to recover from, and\n   even pays a little hype (§5.8).\n4. **Both seasons.** 6 summer + 6 winter events on alternating days; each venue has its own look, light and music.\n5. **Couch first, online too.** 1–4 local players in every mode; AI Hub ghost heats when the hub launches the game.\n\n### 1.3 Genre and perspective (decisions)\n\n- **Genre:** arcade multi-event sports (Track & Field / Winter Games lineage) with a short campaign, local party\n  play and online ghost heats. Each event is a compact mini-game built on one shared event framework.\n- **Perspective:** per event, all on the engine's native 2D views (pixel art at `res: 'ps1'`, `expand: true`):\n  - **2.5D side-on lanes** (`'brawler'` view, pitch 25): 100m Dash, Javelin, 50m Freestyle, Weightlifting.\n  - **Pure side view** (`'side'`): 10m Diving, Ski Jump, the archer's inset.\n  - **Target close-up overlay:** Archery's main view.\n  - **Pseudo-3D behind the athlete** (the `road` module, `E.Road`): Downhill, Bobsled.\n  - **Three-quarter** (`'threequarter'`): Figure Skating, Ice Hockey.\n  - Ceremonies, podiums and the title use `'brawler'` in their venue.\n  - **Top-down** (`'topdown'`): Curling.\n  Rationale: each event gets the camera its classic arcade ancestors used, and the engine has a native, tested view\n  for every one of them.\n\n### 1.4 Core loop\n\nPick nation → (ceremony) → **day card** (who, where, a human-interest segment) → **event card** (one screen: goal and\ncontrols with button glyphs) → **compete** (live vs CPU rivals and friends) → **results** (records, qualifying) →\n**medal ceremony** → **medal table** (story beat) → next day. 12 days, then the closing ceremony and an ending that\ndepends on your nation's rank.\n\n### 1.5 Modes (main menu, in this order)\n\n| Item | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| CONTINUE GAMES | only when an autosave exists: resumes The Games at the next day |\n| THE GAMES | the campaign: opening ceremony, 12 days (all 12 events), story beats, halftime report, closing ceremony, ending; or, chosen on its setup screen, **Quick Games**: 4 events (playlists *Track & Pool*, *Snow & Ice*, *Greatest Hits*, *Random 4*) with mini ceremonies and party points. 1–4 players |\n| SINGLE EVENT | any of the 12 events, vs CPU or practice (no rivals); 1–4 players |\n| RECORDS | world records and top-5 tables per event (initials), the Laurel cabinet, the Medal cabinet |\n| HOW TO PLAY | Basics (mash, timing, hype & turbo, yikes) + every event's card |\n| SETTINGS | the engine's settings screen plus the game's own (§2.5) |\n| ABOUT & CREDITS | Source Information, Testing/Engine/Prompt Feedback, credits, engine changes, controls |\n\nOnline play is not a menu item: it starts only when the AI Hub launches the page (§12.2).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Controls and input (controller-first, keyboard and mouse native)\n\n### 2.1 The action map (custom preset `OLY_KEYS`, replaces the engine presets for the whole game)\n\n| Action | Meaning | DualSense (default glyphs) | Xbox glyphs (setting) | Keyboard | Mouse |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `up/down/left/right` | move, steer, aim, balance, menu focus | left stick, d-pad | left stick, d-pad | WASD, arrows | — |\n| `mashL` | \"left\": left foot/arm, push, pass, tuck (diving), in-turn | □ and L1 | X and LB | **J** | — |\n| `mashR` | \"right\": right foot/arm, push, check, pike (diving), out-turn | ○ and R1 | B and RB | **K** | — |\n| `action` | jump, throw, release, start, take-off, shoot | ✕ | A | **Space** | Left button (aim events only) |\n| `turbo` | fire the YIKES TURBO when the hype flame is full | △ | Y | **Shift** | — |\n| `alt` | hold: tuck, breathe, hold breath, skate burst | R2 (and L2) | RT (and LT) | **L** | Right button (aim events only) |\n| `pause` | pause menu | Options | Menu | Esc, P | — |\n| `confirm` | menus: choose | ✕ | A | Enter, Space | click |\n| `cancel` | menus: back | ○ | B | Esc, Backspace | — |\n\nRules:\n- **`confirm`/`cancel` deliberately do not include J or K** (the engine's DEFAULT preset has them): a sprinter mashing J/K\n  must never skip a results screen. Every screen entered after play has a **0.6 s input lockout** and calls\n  `input.consumeAll()` on enter.\n- **Mash = alternate `mashL` and `mashR`.** PC players mash J/K with the right hand; pad players rock □/○ with a thumb\n  or alternate L1/R1 with index fingers (both pairs are bound). Mash assist (§2.5) offers one-button and hold modes.\n- **Mouse:** menus everywhere (hover moves the focus, click picks; `E.Menu` does this, our widgets copy it). In-world\n  only where the genre uses it: Archery (pointer aims, hold left to draw/release to shoot, hold right to hold breath),\n  Curling (pointer aims the broom target, left button = `action`), Hockey (left: hold/release shoot toward the\n  cursor, right: pass toward the cursor), plus clicking flags on Nation Select and tiles on Single Event. Those event\n  scenes set their own `input` preset that adds `Mouse0`/`Mouse2`; other scenes leave the mouse unbound in play.\n- **Pause and the hub:** in an AI Hub session, \"Create + Options\" belongs to the hub: while pad button 8 (Create) is\n  held, suppress `pause` *before* the engine reads it (needs the exported input hook, §4.6 change 1).\n- Two players on one keyboard: the engine's `game.allowJoin` splits it (P1 WASD + F G H R T Y, P2 arrows + `.` `/` `,`\n  and numpad); our actions map onto the halves in preset order (`mashL, mashR, action, turbo, alt`). Prompts follow\n  automatically because every prompt comes from `input.label(action)`.\n\n### 2.2 Per-event use of the actions\n\n| Event | stick / WASD | mashL □ J | mashR ○ K | action ✕ Space | turbo △ Shift | alt R2 L | mouse |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 100m Dash | — | left foot | right foot | react at the gun; dip at the line | turbo | — | — |\n| Javelin | — | run | run | hold: angle rises; release: throw | turbo | — | — |\n| 50m Freestyle | — | left arm (on the beat) | right arm (on the beat) | start dive, flip turn, touch | turbo | breathe | — |\n| 10m Diving | tap ←/→: half twist | hold: tuck | hold: pike | take-off timing | turbo | — | — |\n| Archery | aim | — | — | hold: draw; release: shoot | turbo | hold: hold breath | pointer aims, L draw, R breath |\n| Weightlifting | ←/→ balance | lift | lift | jerk timing | turbo | — | — |\n| Ski Jump | ↑/↓ balance, body angle | — | — | push off, take-off, telemark | turbo | — | — |\n| Downhill | steer | — | — | pre-jump | turbo | hold: tuck | — |\n| Bobsled | steer | push | push | jump in (load) | turbo | — | — |\n| Figure Skating | ← ↓ ↑ → notes | — | — | hold/release jump notes | turbo | — | — |\n| Curling | aim | in-turn; sweep | out-turn; sweep | start slide; release | turbo | — | pointer aims, L = action |\n| Ice Hockey | skate | pass | check / switch skater | hold: charge, release: shoot | ON FIRE | skate burst | L shoot at cursor, R pass at cursor |\n\n### 2.3 Button prompts and glyphs (a must-build: the pixel font has no ✕ ○ □ △)\n\n`input.label(action)` already returns the right *text* for the player's last device and bindings ('J', 'Space',\n'Left click', '✕', 'A'...), and the engine's `glyphs` setting picks the controller family. But the engine's 5×7 pixel\nfont has no ✕ ○ □ △ (they render as `?`). Build **`O.Prompt`** (src/02-prompts.js):\n\n- `O.Prompt.draw(g, x, y, action, { input = player's input, size: 1|2, label: 'RUN', align })` resolves the code\n  for that player's `lastDevice` from `input.map`/`input.bindings`, then draws an **icon**, never plain text:\n  - PlayStation face buttons: a 9×9 (size 1) / 17×17 (size 2) dark disc with a light rim and the symbol drawn in pixels\n    in its traditional color (✕ blue `#7fb2ff`, ○ red `#ff6b6b`, □ pink `#ff8fd8`, △ green `#4fe0a8`).\n  - Xbox face buttons: disc with the letter (A green `#5bc236`, B red `#e8443a`, X blue `#3a7cf0`, Y yellow `#f2c21b`).\n  - Shoulders/triggers: rounded tab \"L1/R1/L2/R2\" or \"LB/RB/LT/RT\"; Options/Menu: small pill; sticks: a ring with an\n    arrow; d-pad: a cross with the pressed arm lit.\n  - Keyboard: a keycap (rounded rect, 1 px darker bottom edge) with the key's label; Space and Shift are wide caps.\n  - Mouse: a mouse outline with the left/right half filled.\n  - A pair prompt for mashing (`O.Prompt.pair(g, x, y, 'mashL', 'mashR')`) alternates highlight at the player's\n    current mash rhythm (teaches the alternation).\n- Prompts follow the **last input used, per player** (`input.lastDevice`); in multiplayer each lane/turn shows its\n  own player's glyphs.\n- **Default glyph family for controllers: PlayStation.** On first boot, if `game.settings.glyphs` is `'auto'` (never\n  chosen) set it to `'playstation'` (engine change 4). The Settings → Game screen has **Controller prompts:\n  PlayStation / Xbox** (key `promptStyle`) whose `apply` calls `game.settings.set('glyphs', v)`.\n- Also add pixel glyphs for ✕ ○ □ △ to the engine's 5×7 and 3×5 fonts (engine change 3) so any stray label text\n  still reads correctly.\n\n### 2.4 Menus\n\nStick/d-pad/WASD/arrows move the focus (with `input.repeat`); ✕/Enter/Space/click choose; ○/Esc/Backspace go back;\nL1/R1 or Q/E switch tabs (also clickable); hovering with the mouse moves the focus. Every screen shows its prompt strip\nat the bottom (`✕ Select  ○ Back`) with glyph icons.\n\n### 2.5 The game's settings (Settings → Game group, via `new E.Game({ menu: { settings: [...] } })`)\n\n| Key | Label | Options (default **bold**) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `difficulty` | Difficulty | Easy / **Normal** / Hard (CPU skill offset −0.12 / 0 / +0.06; timing windows ×1.25 / 1 / 0.85; qualifying standards per event) |\n| `promptStyle` | Controller prompts | **PlayStation** / Xbox |\n| `mashAssist` | Mash assist | **Off** / One button (any mash button counts as an alternation) / Hold (holding either = steady 72% pace) |\n| `timingAssist` | Timing assist | **Off** / On (all timing windows ×1.4) |\n| `commentary` | Commentary | **Voices + subtitles** / Subtitles only / Off |\n| `textSize` | Text size | **Large** / Huge (×1.5 for subtitles, cards and HUD labels) |\n| `hints` | Hints | **On** / Off (contextual tips, e.g. \"Alternate □ and ○!\") |\n| `voices` | Voices volume (Sound group) | slider 0–1, **0.8** (engine change 6) |\n| `crowd` | Crowd volume (Sound group) | slider 0–1, **0.7** |\n\nThe engine's own Display/Sound/Comfort/Controller/Touch settings, rebinding and full screen stay as they are\n(TASK.md: don't rebuild standard features).\n\n---\n\n## 3. UI and UX (10-foot)\n\n### 3.1 Rules\n\n- **Base resolution** `res: 'ps1'` with `expand: true` (a 16:9 TV shows ~427×240 game pixels, scaled ×4.5 at 1080p).\n  Primary text uses `E.font` at **scale 2** (≈63 px tall on a 1080p TV), secondary at scale 1 (≈31 px); never the\n  `tiny` font for anything a player must read. Titles use `E.font.title` scale 4–5.\n- **At most 7 items per list; at most 8 rows per table** (8 nations / 8 lanes). No scrolling tables, no web-style\n  dense screens; long content is paged (L1/R1, ←/→ or clickable page dots).\n- **Focus is loud:** the focused item has a gold bar, a ▸ cursor, a 1 px glow and a gentle scale pulse; a `select`\n  blip on move, `confirm` on choose.\n- **TV-safe margins:** keep HUD and text ≥ 12 game px from every edge; keep the top-right clear of\n  `game.cornerArea()` (the engine's menu/full-screen buttons).\n- **Anchoring:** every HUD element anchors to `r.W`/`r.H`; wide screens show more venue (more stands, more slope).\n- **Information never in color alone:** players are P1–P4 tags plus color (`E.PLAYER_COLORS`), medals carry 1/2/3.\n- **The engine's HTML screens** (pause, settings, controls) must be TV-readable: inject a stylesheet (no engine change)\n  after the engine creates its shell, e.g. `.esh{font-size:clamp(16px,1.55vw,30px)} .esh button{font-size:1.15em;min-height:2.9em;padding:.7em 1em}\n  .esh h2{font-size:2.2em} .esh-mod{width:min(820px,94vw)} .esh input[type=range]{width:min(320px,30vw);height:2.2em}`\n  and theme it gold-on-navy via `E.Shell` theme variables (`accent: '#f2b632'`, `paper: 'rgba(12,16,40,.92)'`).\n  Check with a 1920×1080 screenshot.\n\n### 3.2 Screens (all pixel art unless marked HTML)\n\n| # | Screen | Layout essentials |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Boot (engine) | `boot: { title: 'OLYMPIYIKES!', steps: [...], messages: ['Inflating the blimp', 'Waxing the skis', 'Teaching the crowd to wave', 'Calming the mascot'] }` |\n| 2 | Title | stadium at sunset (summer half) beside a floodlit ski jump (winter half), cauldron burning, blimp, the 8 athletes warming up in a row, logo `OLYMPIYIKES!` (E.font.title scale 5, gold→orange, red outline, depth 3), emblem, tagline, pulsing \"PRESS ✕\" (glyph by device), engine version tiny bottom-right. Idle 10 s → attract |\n| 3 | Main menu | left: big list (§1.5); right: a live vignette for the focused item (parade / pictogram wheel / trophy / the mascot); bottom: description + prompt strip |\n| 4 | Touch-only notice | replaces \"PRESS ✕\": panel **\"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\"**, one line \"Connect a controller or keyboard to play.\", a big **SETTINGS** button (tap → `game.menu('settings')`). Attract still runs |\n| 5 | Games setup | rows: Length (Full 12 / Quick 4 + playlist), Difficulty, Qualifying (On for 1P / Off), START |\n| 6 | Nation select + join | 4×2 grid of big flags (48×32) with codes; each player's cursor in its color with a P-tag; right panel: the focused nation's athlete (live rig cheering), name, 3 specialty pictograms, one-line bio; \"P2–P4: press ✕ on another controller, or 2 on the keyboard\" |\n| 7 | Opening ceremony | cinematic (§7.4), hold ✕ for 1 s to skip |\n| 8 | Day card (\"broadcast bumper\") | `DAY 3 · 50m FREESTYLE` / venue / weather; lower third: **UP CLOSE & PERSONAL** with a big portrait and 2–3 subtitle lines; optional rival line |\n| 9 | Event card | pictogram + name; GOAL line; 3–4 rows of glyph icon(s) + verb; Qualifying standard, World record; prompts `✕ Start  ○ Back` (+ `△ Practice` in Single Event) |\n| 10 | Event HUD | per event (§6); common: top-left event + pictogram, top-right clock/score (big digits), bottom: per-player prompt strip and the hype flame |\n| 11 | Turn card | \"P2 — YOUR TURN\" in player color / \"ROUND 2 OF 3\" + top-4 standings |\n| 12 | Results | ≤ 8 rows: rank, medal icon, flag, athlete, performance, notes (WR, GR, PB, Q, DNF, DQ); humans' rows in player color; records burst; `✕ Continue` |\n| 13 | Initials entry | `E.Arcade` letter wheel when a human makes a top-5 table (skipped in hub) |\n| 14 | Medal ceremony | podium in the venue, medals, three flags rising, the winner's procedural anthem, fireworks |\n| 15 | Medal table | 8 nation rows (flag, code, G S B, total), yours highlighted; a ticker of the day's highlights |\n| 16 | Story beat | day-card layout with one or two portraits (halftime report, incidents, rival) |\n| 17 | Torch lost / Games over | \"YIKES! NO QUALIFYING MARK — TORCHES ●●○\" → retry; at 0: \"GAMES OVER — CONTINUE? 9\" |\n| 18 | Closing + ending + credits | cinematic, ending text by rank, credits roll (paged, skippable) |\n| 19 | Single Event select | 4×3 grid of event tiles (pictogram, name, season color, your best medal); bottom: description |\n| 20 | Records | tabs per event (←/→ or L1/R1): top-5 rows; tabs LAURELS (12 tiles) and CABINET (nation × event medals as icons) |\n| 21 | How to play | Basics pages + list of 12 event cards (read-only) |\n| 22 | Settings / Controls / Pause | engine HTML (scaled, themed) |\n| 23 | About & Credits | paged: Source Information · Testing Feedback · Engine Feedback · Prompt Feedback · Credits & engine changes · Controls |\n| 24 | Dev panel | pixel overlay (§13) |\n| 25 | Hub card / hub splash | §12.2 |\n\nTransitions: `game.go(scene, data, { fade: 'wipe' })` between menu screens, `'iris'` into events, `'white'` into\nceremonies (reduce-motion turns them into plain fades by itself).\n\n### 3.3 Touch-only devices\n\n`touchOnly = matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches\n&& navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0` **and** no key press or gamepad has been seen this visit. While true: show screen 4,\nhide engine touch buttons (scenes declare `touch: []`; set the engine's `touch` setting to `'off'` at boot),\nlet the attract mode run after 10 s; a tap during attract returns to the notice. A `gamepadconnected` event or any key\npress flips `touchOnly` to false at once and shows the normal title.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Architecture\n\n### 4.1 Tech stack\n\n- **Engine:** our copy of the my-3D2dge v0.85.2 full engine (`engine/my-3d2dge.js`: the core plus every module; we use\n  the `road`, `rhythm`, `physics`, `arcade` and `songs` modules from it). Plain JavaScript, no libraries, no CDN, no\n  network at runtime.\n- **Online:** AI Hub `session.js` 1.4.0, unmodified, first script in `<head>`.\n- **Tooling:** Node (headless tests via `vm`, as `game/test.mjs` does), Playwright 1.63.0 + Chromium (browser checks,\n  hub harness, screenshots), the handoff's `tools/check.mjs` and `tools/filmstrip.mjs`.\n- **Deliverable:** one self-contained HTML (engine + session client + game inlined), ~1.8 MB, works from `file://`.\n\n### 4.2 Folder layout\n\n```\nOlympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837/\n  index.html                 dev page: same <head> as the bundle; loads engine + src files in order (the list is the bundle's source of truth)\n  engine/my-3d2dge.js        the engine + our changes, each marked  // OLY: <why>\n  vendor/hub/                session.js (bundled, unmodified) + harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md (tests only)\n  vendor/my-3d2dge/          sparse clone of the handoff: docs, kits, tools (reference + Playwright); never bundled\n  src/                       the game: one IIFE per file, all attach to window.OLY (alias O)\n  tests/                     run.mjs (the one command) + suites\n  tools/bundle.mjs           builds the root HTML from index.html's script list\n  tools/shots.mjs            screenshot/filmstrip helper around the handoff tools\n```\n\n### 4.3 Source files (load order = bundle order)\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `00-core.js` | creates `window.OLY`, defines `OLY_KEYS` and `GAME_SETTINGS`, then the `E.Game` (§4.4), constants (`M`, palettes), `O.def(kind, id, spec)` registries, `O.bus` (on/emit), `O.store` (E.store wrappers), `O.rng(label)` streams (§4.7), formatting helpers |\n| `01-input.js` | per-scene presets (archery/curling/hockey add mouse), **pilots** (§5.2), `Mash` meter, `O.AutoPlayer` (bot intents → real `input.tap/hold`), idle/any-input tracker, touch-only detection, hub Create+Options guard |\n| `02-prompts.js` | `O.Prompt` glyph renderer (§2.3) |\n| `03-ui.js` | 10-foot widgets: `Menu10` (vertical list), `Grid10` (tile grid), `Tabs`, `Panel`, `Banner` (big stamped words), `Ticker`, `LowerThird`, `Toast`, page dots, number/time formatters; mouse hover/click via `input.pointer()`/`clicked()` |\n| `04-audio.js` | SFX definitions (`audio.define`), songs (§9), `O.Voice` gibberish synth, `O.CrowdAudio`, `O.Anthem` generator, stings |\n| `05-art.js` | palettes per venue, flag painter, pictograms, emblem, equipment sprites, stands + crowd painter, jumbotron (dot matrix), podium, fireworks/confetti helpers, mascot (Blob) |\n| `06-pose.js` | `O.Pose` library and `O.Gear` (equipment drawn at joints), body rotation (§8.2) |\n| `07-athletes.js` | `NATIONS` data (§7.1), teammates, `O.makeRig(nation, sport, opts)` outfits per sport, voice params |\n| `08-commentary.js` | `O.Comms`: commentators, line banks (§7.6), cue rules, subtitles + voice + portraits |\n| `09-hype.js` | `O.Hype` (meter, turbo), `O.Yikes` (stamp, count, sympathy hype), `O.Crowd` (visual excitement), slow-mo/photo helpers |\n| `10-records.js` | world records seed table, games records, personal bests, top-5 tables via `E.Arcade`, points formulas, medal table, party points, laurels, cabinet |\n| `11-ghosts.js` | ghost recording/playback (local turns + hub), compact samples |\n| `12-eventkit.js` | the event contract, `O.defEvent`, the phase runner, formats (race / attempts / match / program), CPU simulation, results assembly, qualifying, timing widgets (`TimingBar`, `Ring`, `Balance`, `Sway`, `StrokeBeat`) |\n| `20-ev-sprint.js` … `35-ev-hockey.js` | one file per event (§6), ids: `sprint javelin swim diving archery weights skijump downhill bobsled figure curling hockey` |\n| `40-sc-title.js` | title, main menu, touch-only notice, attract director (§11) |\n| `41-sc-games.js` | games setup, nation select/join, opening ceremony, day card, story beats, event card, turn card, results, initials, medal ceremony, medal table, torch/continue, closing + ending + credits |\n| `42-sc-misc.js` | single event select, records, how to play, about & credits, pose lab |\n| `43-dev.js` | dev panel, tuning sliders, cheats, overlays (§13) |\n| `44-hub.js` | AI Hub session flow (§12.2) |\n| `99-main.js` | registers scenes, deep links (`#ev/<id>`, `#scene/<name>`, `#attract`, `#poselab`, `#games/day/<n>`), `game.debug`, `window.__oly` for tests, `game.start({ scenes, scene, boot })` |\n\nEach file: `(() => { 'use strict'; const E = My3D2dge, O = OLY; ... })();`. Tests load exactly the same files in the same\norder into a `vm` context (read the list from `index.html` so it can't drift).\n\n### 4.4 The game object\n\n```js\nconst game = O.game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'brawler', input: OLY_KEYS,\n  id: 'olympiyikes', bg: '#0b0f24',\n  menu: { items: inHub ? [] : [['Restart event', () => O.restartEvent()], ['How to play', () => O.showEventCard()], ['Dev mode', () => O.Dev.open()]],\n          settings: GAME_SETTINGS /* §2.5 */, quit: inHub ? false : 'title',\n          controls: { mashL: 'Left (mash, pass, tuck)', mashR: 'Right (mash, check, pike)', action: 'Action (jump, throw, release)',\n                      turbo: 'Yikes Turbo', alt: 'Hold (tuck, breathe, steady)' } } });\n```\n`inHub = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active)` (true from the client's first line). `OLY_KEYS` and `GAME_SETTINGS` are defined\nin `00-core.js` above this call (the later files only add to them); the menu callbacks are arrows because their targets\nare defined in later files. Menu items are static, so each item's\nfunction is context-aware: outside an event \"Restart event\" and \"How to play\" show `game.note('Not in an event')`.\n\n### 4.5 Scenes\n\n`O.scene(name, def)` registers a wrapped engine scene. The wrapper: calls `input.consumeAll()` on enter; applies the\n0.6 s lockout (`def.lock`); if the dev panel is open, runs `O.Dev.update()` instead of `def.update` and draws the panel\nafter `def.draw`; draws global overlays (toasts, commentary lower third, attract banner, \"YIKES\" stamps, laurel toasts)\nafter the scene; tracks idle time on menu scenes (`def.menu: true`) for the attract mode; routes `back()`.\n\nScenes: `title`, `menu`, `touchonly` (a state of `title`), `attract`, `gamesSetup`, `nations`, `opening`, `dayCard`,\n`beat`, `eventCard`, `turnCard` (overlay state inside events), `ev:<id>` ×12, `results`, `initials`, `podium`,\n`medals`, `torch`, `closing`, `credits`, `single`, `records`, `howto`, `about`, `poselab`, `hubCard`, `hubSplash`.\n\n`O.flow` is the state machine above them: it holds the current **meet** (§4.8) and decides the next scene after each\none ends (`O.flow.next(from, payload)`), for each mode (games, quick, single, hub, attract).\n\n### 4.6 Engine changes (all marked `// OLY:` in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`; list them on the About screen)\n\n1. **Export the hooks:** `E.HOOKS = HOOKS;` so the game can run code at the start of every step even while paused\n   (`HOOKS.input`): hub Create+Options guard, global any-input detection.\n2. **Cosmetic randomness off `Math.random`:** the Humanoid (`this.t` start phase, blink timer), `Particles` and\n   `hitFx`'s number jitter draw from a module-level `const cosmetic = rng(0xC05E7)` instead of `Math.random`. Then\n   cosmetics never shift gameplay randomness, the hub card draws no `Math.random` numbers, and tests stay\n   deterministic.\n3. **Font glyphs:** add ✕ ○ □ △ to the 5×7 (`G57`) and 3×5 (`GLYPHS`) tables.\n4. **PlayStation by default:** the `glyphs` setting's default becomes `'playstation'`.\n5. **Pose hook on the Humanoid:** at the end of `solvePose()`, if `this.post` is a function call `this.post(this, this.J)`;\n   then, if `this.bodyPitch || this.bodyRoll`, rotate every joint (and cape/hair points, as `_roll` does) about\n   `this.pivot` (default: hip centre) by pitch (forward–up plane) and roll (right–up plane), **without** `_roll`'s\n   floor lift. This is what flips, dives, swims, tumbles and V-style flight need (§8.2).\n6. **Voice bus:** `ChipAudio` gets a `_voiceBus` gain under the master, a `voiceVolume` field honored by\n   `applyVolume()`, and the settings get `voices` (Sound group, default .8). `O.Voice` connects to it.\n\n### 4.7 Randomness and determinism\n\n- **Gameplay randomness only through labeled streams:** `O.rng(label)` returns a `[0,1)` generator. In a hub session\n  it is `AIHub.rng(label)` (identical on every copy); otherwise `E.rng(hash(meet.seed + '|' + label))`. Labels are\n  namespaced: `'sprint:gun'`, `'javelin:wind:r2'`, `'cpu:FRM:skijump:j1'`, `'judges:diving:SUN:d3'`.\n- Cosmetics (particles, blinks, crowd bob) never touch `Math.random` (engine change 2) or the gameplay streams.\n- `meet.seed` comes from the clock when a meet starts; tests and the dev panel can set it.\n- Every event sim is a function of (state, intents, streams), independent of drawing, so a sim can run headless,\n  twice, and hash the same (the kits' \"proof\" idea).\n\n### 4.8 Data model\n\n```\nNation   { id: 'SUN', name: 'SUNVALE', colors: { a, b, c }, flag: { kind, ... }, athlete: { name, rig, bio, voice },\n           team: [3 names], skills: { sprint: .92, ... }, anthem: { seed, key, bpm } }\nAthlete  { id, nation, name, rig, gear, pilot, lane, human, player (0-3 | null), hype, turboT, state: {}, attempts: [],\n           best, notes: [], ghost }\nPilot    { kind: 'human' | 'bot' | 'ghost' | 'net', input?, skill, cheat?: 'perfect' | null }\nIntent   { L, R, A, T (pressed this step), Lh, Rh, Ad, Au, X (held / released), mv: [x, y], aim: [x, y] | null }\nMeet     { mode, seed, events: [ids], day, players: [{ input, nation, color }], difficulty, qualifying, torches,\n           medals: { SUN: { g, s, b } }, party: { P1: pts }, results: { eventId: Results }, beats: Set, yikes: { SUN: n } }\nResults  { event, rows: [{ athlete, perf, display, rank, medal, notes, points }], records: [], laurels: [] }\nStore    'oly:records' (top-5 per event + WR), 'oly:laurels', 'oly:cabinet', 'oly:games' (autosave),\n         'oly:ghost:<event>' (best local run), 'oly:seen' (first-time tips), 'oly:tune' (only if the dev opts in)\n```\n\n### 4.9 Bundle\n\n`node tools/bundle.mjs` reads `index.html`'s `<script src>` list and writes the root HTML:\n\n```html\n<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>/* vendor/hub/session.js, byte-for-byte */</script>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>Olympiyikes! — Faster. Higher. Yikes.</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Twelve over-the-top Summer and Winter events in one wild fortnight, for 1–4 players.\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#f2b632\"><link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:image/svg+xml,...the emblem...\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"><meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Score the most points across three Olympiyikes events\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move · □○ or J K mash · ✕/Space act · △/Shift turbo · R2/L hold\">\n<meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"The Olympic Games\"><meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"(the building model's id)\">\n<style>/* page + 10-foot shell overrides */</style></head><body>\n<!-- E.bootSplash('OLYMPIYIKES!') markup --><canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n<script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js */</script><script>/* src/*.js concatenated */</script></body></html>\n```\nEscape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\/script`. The session client must stay unmodified and first after\n`<meta charset>`. The bundle test (§16) checks all of this.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Shared gameplay systems\n\n### 5.1 The event contract (`O.defEvent`) and the phase runner\n\nEvery event is one call. The EventKit turns it into an engine scene `ev:<id>`, registers it in `O.EVENTS`, its\ntunables in the tuning registry (§5.13), its card in How to Play, its segment in the attract playlist and, if\n`hub.ok`, in the hub deal.\n\n```js","numLines":440,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1723}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SSXQFahn9C5fLWiohqULeq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
