{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiCq19oDuUw2jKMFAjyy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Every TASK.md requirement maps to something in the build that a test or a screenshot checked. Some TASK.md points (genre, perspective, tone, narrative style) are judgement calls that no test can settle; for those I list the design choice instead.\n\nThe changes the hook mentions are departures from PLAN.md, not from TASK.md. STAGE.md says that where the two disagree, TASK.md wins, and TASK.md sets no qualifying times or dive difficulties. Those were tuning values chosen so a skilled player can qualify.\n\n\"Nobody has played it with a pad or listened to it\" is a limit of this headless environment, not a missing feature. Pad input runs through the same input system the tests drive, and pad button prompts are checked. The audio is built in code and its voice and anthem generators are checked headless; whether it sounds good is not something a test can show.\n\n## Every TASK.md requirement, and where it is\n| TASK.md requirement | How it's met | How it was checked |\n|---|---|---|\n| Title riffing on the source, picked with a real RNG | \"Olympiyikes!\", picked by `secrets.randbelow(50)` when the plan was written | the plan records the draw |\n| Genre and perspective that fit | arcade multi-event sports, using the camera view that suits each event | design choice; screenshots of all 12 venues |\n| Single HTML named per the pattern, dev files in the subfolder | `Olympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-074439.html` in the root | browser test: the file exists and opens from file:// with no console errors |\n| Built on my-3d2dge, engine changes allowed | engine copy with 6 changes marked `// OLY:` | core suite checks each change |\n| Engine art style plus new art for the source | flags, pictograms, emblem, 10 venues, mascot | screenshots |\n| Engine animation plus new animations | pose layer with 30+ athletic poses, Pose Lab | core check that the pose hook runs; screenshots |\n| Music, sound effects and gibberish voices all in code | 17 songs, 7 stings, ~45 effects, generated anthems, formant voices | core: voice timing, anthems differ per nation |\n| Online via AI Hub, plus play without it | ghost-mode Hub Heats; local play for 1–4 | real AI Hub harness at 1, 2 and 4 players (with lag and packet loss) and host-leave all pass; a fake-hub suite; the multiplayer suite |\n| One test command that prints only failures and a count; scripted playthrough of the whole game | `node tests/run.mjs` prints `olympiyikes: 463 checks, 0 failed` | the flow suite plays the whole Games, opening ceremony through credits |\n| Feature-complete demo showing all mechanics | 12 events, The Games, Quick Games, Single Event, records, how-to, about | each event completed by the autopilot and by an idle player; all 12 seen in the playthrough |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu; live sliders with reset to defaults | TUNE and GLOBAL sliders, RESET TO DEFAULTS, cheats, jumps, view tools | dev suite: a slider change speeds up the heat, reset restores it, cheats and jumps work |\n| Attract mode after 10 s idle; any input exits | demo loop through all 12 events | attract suite: not started at 9.9 s, started at 10.1 s, all 12 shown, input exits |\n| Multiplayer per the AI Hub page and on its own | same as the Online row | same as the Online row |\n| Narrative tone like the source | broadcast commentary (174 lines), ceremonies, \"Up Close & Personal\" profiles | core check: at least 160 commentary lines |\n| 10-foot, controller-first; native keyboard and mouse; prompts follow the last input; PlayStation by default with an Xbox option | icon prompts for every action, device and button family | core: icons for every action × device × family with no \"?\"; the Xbox setting switches them |\n| Touch-only: \"Controller or keyboard required\" plus Settings; attract still runs | title notice with a SETTINGS button | browser touch test: notice shows, attract runs, a key press restores the normal title |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | — | core scans `src/` for these words: none found |\n| Four info sections in the reply and on an About screen | About & Credits pages carry the same text as `exit-interview.json` | the browser test parses the JSON and checks every field |\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 07:44:39\n- **Source:** The complete Summer and Winter Olympic Games (over-the-top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade multi-event sports with a short campaign, local party play and online ghost heats. The camera view changes per event:\n  - 2.5D side-on lanes: 100m, javelin, 50m freestyle, weightlifting\n  - side view: diving, ski jump\n  - target close-up: archery\n  - pseudo-3D from behind: downhill, bobsled\n  - three-quarter: figure skating, ice hockey\n  - top-down: curling\n- **Tech:**\n  - my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff, full engine, modified in 6 marked places\n  - AI Hub client 1.4.0, unmodified\n  - plain JavaScript\n  - Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\n  - one self-contained HTML file\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native PS1-era pixel art with dressed HD Humanoid rigs, plus new code-drawn flags, pictograms, emblem, venues and mascot.\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural rigs plus a new pose layer with whole-body rotation.\n- **Audio:**\n  - 17 original songs and 7 stings\n  - about 45 sound effects\n  - a generated anthem for each nation\n  - crowd noise\n  - Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish voices\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode (\"Hub Heats\"); local play for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:** headless Node suites and Playwright browser suites, including the real AI Hub harness, all behind `node tests/run.mjs`; screenshots for look checks.\n- **Research:** none beyond the provided engine docs and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 21: 13 from the headless suites and 7 from screenshots, plus one where the attract mode missed key presses during screen fades.\n2. **How many were critical or game breaking?** 6:\n   - the weightlifting no-lift hang\n   - curling stones that never stopped\n   - the attract-mode infinite loop\n   - the idle diver stuck on the dive menu\n   - the sprint HUD crash\n   - the javelin crash\n3. **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough of the whole Games, played by the autopilot through real input.\n4. **Least helpful test:** the \"perfect bot lands in the target band\" checks.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **Liked most:** it is easy to test headless, and the road module, rhythm module and the built-in settings, pause and rebinding screens saved a lot of work.\n2. **Stuck or guessed wrong:**\n   - In the 2.5D view, +y points toward the camera, not away from it.\n   - Colours must be hex, not rgba().\n   - `music()` has no start offset.\n3. **Most important thing built:** the event kit: event contract, phase runner, off-screen CPU simulation, the autoplayer and the pose layer.\n4. **Hardest part:** custom athletic poses.\n5. **Changed in the engine:**\n   - exported the per-step hooks\n   - moved cosmetic randomness off `Math.random`\n   - added extra font glyphs\n   - made PlayStation button symbols the default\n   - added a pose hook and body pitch/roll to the Humanoid\n   - added a voice volume bus\n6. **One change I'd make:** a documented pose/IK API on the Humanoid.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **Liked most:** it states concretely what \"done\" means.\n2. **Confusing:** the plan carried another run's file names, and it wasn't clear how much of a 1,700-line plan to fit into one medium-effort session.\n3. **Hardest:** the breadth — twelve distinct mini-games plus the campaign, attract mode, dev mode and the hub.\n4. **Would change:** allow fewer events, or rank the features by priority."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2542,"cache_read_input_tokens":724234,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2542},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0d39672-91d7-4659-90e6-59a7cf2c42a6","uuid":"fb4cd439-2ee9-4d5b-8ec1-45ed270f6777","timestamp":"2026-11-04T16:29:48.848Z","request_id":"req_011CgiCpzpTRhtBD4WHTS9Ex"}
