{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiD5RioNAjabFQKNBeJN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've put the two plan numbers back and rebuilt; the full suite now reads **465 checks, 0 failed**.\n\n- **Bobsled qualifying** is back to the plan's 92 / 86 / 82 s (Easy / Normal / Hard). Since I smoothed the ideal racing line, a skilled bot runs about 42.8 s per run, which clears the Normal mark.\n- **The hardest dive** is back to the plan's 10 half-somersaults, renamed **YIKES! Armstand Quintuple**. The diver starts upside down from a handstand, so ten half-turns still end in a head-first entry. The perfect bot now gets five 10s for 144.00 points, which meets the plan's target of 140 or more. To get there I made the diving simulation use the game's own 1/120 s step and had the bot open up at whichever moment lands closest to vertical.\n- **New gamepad test:** a scripted controller using standard button codes (□/○ to run, ✕ for the action button) drives the sprinter down the track. That's the 2 new checks.\n- **One thing a test can't settle:** whether the generated music and gibberish voices sound good. The generators exist and are tested for timing and for giving each nation a different anthem, but nobody has listened to them.\n\nThe deliverable and `exit-interview.json` were both regenerated after these changes; the JSON parses with every field filled in.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 07:44:39\n- **Source:** The complete Summer and Winter Olympic Games (over-the-top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade multi-event sports with a short campaign, local party play and online ghost heats. Each event uses the camera that suits it:\n  - 2.5D side-on lanes: 100m, javelin, 50m freestyle, weightlifting\n  - side view: diving, ski jump\n  - target close-up: archery\n  - pseudo-3D from behind the athlete: downhill, bobsled\n  - three-quarter: figure skating, ice hockey\n  - top-down: curling\n- **Tech:**\n  - my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff, full engine, with 6 marked changes\n  - AI Hub client 1.4.0, unmodified\n  - plain JavaScript, no libraries\n  - Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\n  - one self-contained HTML file\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native PS1-era pixel art, with dressed character rigs. New art drawn in code:\n  - flags\n  - pictograms\n  - emblem\n  - venues\n  - mascot\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural rigs plus a new pose layer that can rotate the whole body.\n- **Audio:**\n  - 17 original songs and 7 stings\n  - about 45 sound effects\n  - an anthem generated for each nation\n  - crowd noise\n  - Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish voices\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode (\"Hub Heats\"); local play for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:** headless Node suites and Playwright browser suites, including the real AI Hub harness, all behind `node tests/run.mjs`; screenshots for look checks.\n- **Research:** none beyond the provided engine docs and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 21: 13 from the headless suites, 7 from screenshots, and one where the attract mode missed key presses during screen fades.\n2. **How many were critical or game breaking?** 6:\n   - the weightlifting hang\n   - curling stones that never stopped\n   - the attract-mode infinite loop\n   - the idle diver stuck on the dive menu\n   - the sprint HUD crash\n   - the javelin crash\n3. **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough of the whole Games, played by the autopilot through real input.\n4. **Least helpful test:** the \"perfect bot lands in the target band\" checks.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **Liked most:** easy headless testing; the road and rhythm modules; settings, pause and rebinding screens for free.\n2. **Stuck or guessed wrong:**\n   - in the 2.5D view, +y points toward the camera\n   - colours must be hex, not rgba()\n   - `music()` has no start offset\n3. **Most important thing built:** the event kit: the event contract, the phase runner, off-screen CPU simulation, the autoplayer and the pose layer.\n4. **Hardest part:** custom athletic poses.\n5. **Changed in the engine:**\n   - exported the per-step hooks\n   - moved cosmetic randomness off `Math.random`\n   - added font glyphs\n   - made PlayStation button symbols the default\n   - added a pose hook and body pitch/roll to the character rig\n   - added a voice volume bus\n6. **One change I'd make:** a documented pose/IK API on the character rig.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **Liked most:** it states concretely what \"done\" means.\n2. **Confusing:** the plan carried another run's file names, and it wasn't clear how much of a 1,700-line plan fits one medium-effort session.\n3. **Hardest:** the breadth: twelve distinct mini-games plus the campaign, attract mode, dev mode and the hub.\n4. **Would change:** allow fewer events, or rank the features by priority."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":392,"cache_read_input_tokens":737931,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":392},"output_tokens":770,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0d39672-91d7-4659-90e6-59a7cf2c42a6","uuid":"0101549b-c2d2-44ac-8f72-3174427e0832","timestamp":"2026-11-04T16:32:51.935Z","request_id":"req_011CgiD5RLjEMcgKCL3Ngm9s"}
