{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiDJe4pDi8XHjWYn2C39","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the last real gap: the engine's settings screen was still too small at 1080p. After rebuilding, the full suite reads **465 checks, 0 failed**.\n\n- **Settings screen at 1080p:** I scaled up the remaining small text too: the grey help lines and the slider percentages. In a 1920×1080 screenshot, the labels, buttons, help text and percentages are all readable from the couch. A scan of the page found no text below 16 px.\n- **Audio in a real browser:** on the bundled game in Chromium, the first key press starts sound (the audio system reports \"running\"). In 9 seconds of the 100m dash, music was playing, 355 tones and 199 noise sounds were created (music, effects, voices, crowd), and the voice channel was on at 80%. Whether the music and voices sound good still needs a human to listen; no test can judge that.\n- **Gamepad and prompts:** tests drive the sprint with standard gamepad buttons (□/○ to run, ✕ for action). Button prompts are checked for every action on keyboard, mouse and gamepad, in PlayStation and Xbox symbols. The prompts follow the device you used last; that is checked with keyboard, mouse and gamepad as the last device.\n- **Deliverables:** `Olympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-074439.html` and `exit-interview.json` are in the folder root. The JSON was regenerated with this build, parses, and fills every field.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 07:44:39\n- **Source:** The complete Summer and Winter Olympic Games (over-the-top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade multi-event sports with a short campaign, local party play and online ghost heats. Each event uses the camera that suits it:\n  - 2.5D side-on lanes: 100m, javelin, 50m freestyle, weightlifting\n  - side view: diving, ski jump\n  - target close-up: archery\n  - pseudo-3D from behind: downhill, bobsled\n  - three-quarter: figure skating, ice hockey\n  - top-down: curling\n- **Tech:**\n  - my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff, full engine, with 6 marked changes\n  - AI Hub client 1.4.0, unmodified\n  - plain JavaScript\n  - Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\n  - one self-contained HTML file\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native PS1-era pixel art with dressed rigs, plus new art drawn in code: flags, pictograms, an emblem, venues and a mascot.\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural rigs plus a new pose layer with whole-body rotation.\n- **Audio:**\n  - 17 original songs and 7 stings\n  - about 45 sound effects\n  - a generated anthem per nation\n  - crowd noise\n  - Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish voices\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode (\"Hub Heats\"); local play for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:** headless Node suites and Playwright browser suites, including the real AI Hub harness, all run by `node tests/run.mjs`; screenshots to check the look.\n- **Research:** none beyond the provided engine docs and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 21: 13 from the headless suites, 7 from screenshots, and the attract mode missing key presses during screen fades.\n2. **How many would be considered critical / game breaking?** 6:\n   - the weightlifting hang\n   - curling stones that never stopped\n   - the attract-mode infinite loop\n   - the idle diver stuck on the dive menu\n   - the sprint HUD crash\n   - the javelin crash\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The scripted playthrough of the whole Games, with the autopilot playing through real input.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** The \"perfect bot lands in the target band\" checks.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** Easy headless testing; the road and rhythm modules; settings, pause and rebinding come for free.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?**\n   - +y points toward the camera in the 2.5D view.\n   - Colours must be hex, not rgba().\n   - `music()` has no start offset.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The event kit: the event contract, the phase runner, off-screen CPU simulation, the autoplayer and the pose layer.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Custom athletic poses.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?**\n   - Exported the per-step hooks.\n   - Moved cosmetic randomness off `Math.random`.\n   - Added font glyphs (✕ ○ □ △ and punctuation).\n   - Made PlayStation button symbols the default.\n   - Added a pose hook and body pitch/roll to the character rig.\n   - Added a voice volume bus.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** A documented pose/IK API on the character rig.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** It says concretely what \"done\" means.\n2. **What was confusing?** The plan carried another run's file names, and it wasn't clear how much of a 1,700-line plan fits one medium-effort session.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** The breadth: twelve distinct mini-games, plus the campaign, attract mode, dev mode and the hub.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Allow fewer events, or rank the features by priority."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":435,"cache_read_input_tokens":748661,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":435},"output_tokens":770,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0d39672-91d7-4659-90e6-59a7cf2c42a6","u