gs, 7 stings, about 45 sound effects, generated anthems, crowd noise, gibberish voices — all made in code.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode; local play for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:** headless and Playwright suites behind `node tests/run.mjs`; screenshots.\n- **Research:** none beyond the provided docs.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 21.\n2. **How many were critical or game breaking?** 6: the weightlifting hang, curling stones that never stopped, the attract-mode loop, the stuck diver, the sprint HUD crash and the javelin crash.\n3. **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough of the whole Games through real input.\n4. **Least helpful test:** the \"perfect bot lands in the target band\" checks.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **Liked most:** easy headless testing; the road and rhythm modules; the standard settings, pause and rebinding screens come for free.\n2. **Stuck or guessed wrong:** in the 2.5D view +y points toward the camera; colours must be hex; `music()` has no start offset.\n3. **Most important thing built:** the event kit and the pose layer.\n4. **Hardest part:** custom athletic poses.\n5. **Changed in the engine:** exported the per-step hooks, cosmetic randomness on its own stream, extra font glyphs, PlayStation button symbols by default, a pose hook with body rotation, a voice volume channel.\n6. **One change I'd make:** a documented pose/IK API on the character rig.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **Liked most:** it states concretely what \"done\" means.\n2. **Confusing:** file names left over from another run in the plan, and how much of a 1,700-line plan one medium-effort session should cover.\n3. **Hardest:** the breadth — 12 mini-games plus all the systems around them.\n4. **Would change:** allow fewer events, or rank the features by priority."}],"container":