el art with dressed rigs, plus new code-drawn art.\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural rigs plus a new pose layer.\n- **Audio:** all in code:\n  - 17 songs and 7 stings\n  - about 45 sound effects\n  - generated anthems\n  - crowd noise\n  - gibberish voices\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode; local play for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:** headless and Playwright suites behind `node tests/run.mjs`; screenshots.\n- **Research:** none beyond the provided docs.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 21.\n2. **How many would be considered critical / game breaking?** 6:\n   - the weightlifting hang\n   - curling stones that never stopped\n   - the attract-mode loop\n   - the stuck diver\n   - the sprint HUD crash\n   - the javelin crash\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The scripted playthrough of the whole Games through real input.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** The \"perfect bot lands in the target band\" checks.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** Headless testing; the road and rhythm modules; settings, pause and rebinding come for free.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?**\n   - +y points toward the camera in the 2.5D view.\n   - Colours must be hex, not rgba().\n   - `music()` has no start offset.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The event kit and the pose layer.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Custom athletic poses.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?**\n   - Exported the per-step hooks, for the hub's controller guard and input detection.\n   - Gave visual-only randomness its own stream, so tests and hub cards stay repeatable.\n   - Added font glyphs, so button symbols draw.\n   - Made PlayStation button symbols the default, as TASK.md asks.\n   - Added a pose hook with body rotation, for dives, swims and ski flight.\n   - Added a voice volume channel.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** A documented pose/IK API on the character rig.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** It says concretely what \"done\" means.\n2. **What was confusing?** The plan's leftover file names from another run, and how much of a 1,700-line plan one medium-effort session should cover.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** The breadth: twelve mini-games plus all the systems around them.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Allow fewer events, or rank the features by priority."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1919,"cache_read_input_tokens":751462,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1919},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0d39672-91d7-4659-90e6-59a7cf2c42a6","uuid":"749b0843-627c-4cdc-a9a5-9a76ab4ecba1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T16:36:26.783Z","request_id":"req_011CgiDMDDffK3Zj26WdGZxe"}
