eyond the provided docs\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 21.\n2. **How many were critical or game breaking?** 6.\n3. **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough of the whole Games.\n4. **Least helpful test:** the checks that a perfect-playing bot lands within a set score range.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** headless testing, and the road and rhythm modules.\n2. **Where I got stuck or guessed wrong:**\n   - which way +y points in the 2.5D view\n   - colours have to be hex\n   - `music()` has no start offset\n3. **Most important thing I had to build:** the shared event framework and the pose layer.\n4. **Hardest part:** custom athletic poses.\n5. **What I changed in the engine:** six changes, all marked `// OLY:`:\n   - exported the engine's per-step hooks\n   - a separate random stream for cosmetic effects\n   - new font glyphs\n   - PlayStation button symbols as the default\n   - a pose hook with whole-body rotation\n   - a volume control for voices\n6. **One change I'd make:** a documented pose/IK API.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** the concrete definition of done.\n2. **What was confusing:** the plan carried another run's file names, and it was unclear how much of a 1,700-line plan fits one session at medium effort.\n3. **Hardest thing to do:** the breadth — 12 events plus all the systems around them.\n4. **What I'd change:** allow fewer events, or rank the features by priority."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1420,"cache_read_input_tokens":758599,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1420},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_trans